From 8be62bc95f6f716ebcfcaaa698d4f44fd470e699 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Costa <bruno.costa@cat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:49:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] torqued: enable lateral accel factor learning for Honda
 (audit2 D-2)

Backport of upstream openpilot 839a77334 (#35936), which was already in
09aa21390 when the Honda City 7G was merged upstream. torqued only learns
when CP.lateralTuning is 'torque'; in v0.9.9 the City is the only Honda
with torque tuning, so the PID-tuned Hondas (and the Honda process-replay
segments) keep useParams=False and are unaffected. The override.toml
values [1.2, 1.2, 0.23] remain the starting point, as upstream.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 selfdrive/locationd/torqued.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/selfdrive/locationd/torqued.py b/selfdrive/locationd/torqued.py
index 5ed86e457..9984c2e5e 100755
--- a/selfdrive/locationd/torqued.py
+++ b/selfdrive/locationd/torqued.py
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ MIN_BUCKET_POINTS = np.array([100, 300, 500, 500, 500, 500, 300, 100])
 MIN_ENGAGE_BUFFER = 2  # secs
 
 VERSION = 1  # bump this to invalidate old parameter caches
-ALLOWED_CARS = ['toyota', 'hyundai', 'rivian']
+ALLOWED_CARS = ['toyota', 'hyundai', 'rivian', 'honda']
 
 
 def slope2rot(slope):
-- 
